      "content": "I must strongly advise against self-treating vision changes with unprescribed medications because your symptoms could indicate a medical emergency. Since your symptoms are linked to screen time, taking regular breaks, following the 20-20-20 rule (every 20 minutes, look at something 20 feet away for 20 seconds), and ensuring good lighting when working might help temporarily relieve strain. However, these suggestions are not a substitute for professional medical diagnosis.",
      "source": "target",
